Section - Foyer

Foyer is a room. "A narrow entrance hall with high ceilings, its dark hexagonal floor tiles worn smooth in the middle where generations of feet have passed. A coat rack with a mirror stands beside the door, a single winter coat hanging from it. In the corner, a small telephone table holds a black Bakelite telephone. The bathroom door stands to the west[if bathroom door is closed], closed[end if]. The heavy front door, its upper half frosted glass, leads outside. The hallway continues to the north."
The Foyer is south of Hallway.

[=== ITEMS ===]
The telephone is scenery.
The coat rack is scenery.
The winter coat is scenery.
The table is scenery.

The front door is a door.
The front door is unlocked.
The front door is scenery.
The description of the front door is "A heavy door, its upper half frosted glass."

[=== ARCHITECTURE ===]
The front door is south of the Foyer and north of the Stairwell

The telephone is in the Foyer.
The coat rack is in the Foyer.
The winter coat is in the Foyer.
The table is in the Foyer.

Section - Bathroom

[=== DESCRIPTION ===]
Bathroom is a room. "A small, cold bathroom. White tiles with a border of dark blue halfway up the wall. A claw-foot bathtub dominates the room, a rubber hand shower coiled over the tap. Above the washbasin, a mirror reflects the overhead light. A gas water heater ticks quietly on the wall. A small frosted window lets in a pale rectangle of afternoon light. The foyer lies to the east."

[=== ITEMS ===]
The bathroom door is a door.
The bathroom door is closed.
The bathroom door is scenery.

The washbasin is scenery.
The gas water heater is scenery.
The bathtub is scenery.
The hand shower is scenery.

The printed name of the bathroom mirror is "mirror".
Understand "mirror" as the bathroom mirror.
The description of the bathroom mirror is "A rectangular mirror above the washbasin, framed in white tile."

Instead of searching the bathroom mirror:
	say "A day's worth of stubble. But the face looking back at you is one you can live with. The eyes are sharp, and that's what counts."

[=== ARCHITECTURE ===]
The bathroom door is west of Foyer and east of Bathroom.
The bathroom mirror is scenery in the Bathroom.
The washbasin is in the Bathroom.
The gas water heater is in the Bathroom.
The bathtub is in the Bathroom.
The hand shower is in the Bathroom.

Section - Hallway

Hallway is a room. "A long, narrow hallway running through the heart of the apartment. A worn runner covers the floorboards, its pattern faded to near-invisibility. A single ceiling lamp casts a warm but insufficient light. Doors lead to the bedroom to the west, the dining room to the east, and the kitchen to the north. The foyer opens to the south."

Section - Kitchen

[=== DESCRIPTION ===]
Kitchen is a room. "A narrow kitchen smelling faintly of coffee and old wood. A cast-iron stove stands against one wall, its surface scrubbed clean. Wooden cabinets line the walls above a stone sink. A small table with two chairs sits beneath the window, which looks out onto the rear courtyard.[if the handwritten note is on the table] A note is propped against the salt shaker.[end if] [if pantry door is closed]A plain wooden door leads west[otherwise]An open door leads west[end if]. The hallway lies to the south."
Kitchen is north of Hallway.
The pantry door is west of Kitchen and east of Pantry.

[=== ITEMS ===]
The pantry door is a door.
The pantry door is locked.
The pantry door is scenery.
Understand "door" or "pantry door" as the pantry door.
The description of the pantry door is "A plain wooden door, its paint worn at the edges. A small keyhole sits below the handle."

The cast-iron stove is scenery.

The chairs are scenery.

Understand "chair" as the chairs.

The kitchen table is scenery.
The description of the kitchen table is "A small table, wiped clean. Two chairs. The housekeeper has been here.[if the handwritten note is on the kitchen table] A note leans against the salt shaker, where she left it.[end if]"

The pantry key is undescribed.
Understand "key" or "small key" or "iron key" as the pantry key.
The description of the pantry key is "A small iron key, worn smooth from years of use."
The pantry key unlocks the pantry door.

The kitchen cabinets are a scenery supporter.
The description of the kitchen cabinets is "Wooden cabinets lining the walls above the sink, painted white and worn at the edges.[if the pantry key is on the kitchen cabinets] A small key sits on top of the nearest one.[end if]"

Instead of searching the kitchen cabinets:
	if the pantry key is nowhere:
		now the pantry key is on the kitchen cabinets;
		say "You run your hand along the top of the nearest cabinet. Your fingers find a small key.";
	otherwise:
		say "Nothing else up there."

The handwritten note is a document.
The handwritten note is undescribed.
The description of the handwritten note is "A receipt from the Viktualienmarkt, turned over. On the back, a few lines in a neat, economical hand."
Instead of reading the handwritten note:
	say "Der Herr von nebenan hat wieder nach Ihnen gefragt. Ich habe gesagt, Sie sind beschäftigt. Die Post liegt auf Ihrem Schreibtisch. Bin morgen früh wieder da. – F. [line break][line break][italic type](The gentleman next door has been asking for you again. I told him you were busy. The post is on your desk. Back tomorrow morning. – F.)[roman type][line break][line break]Wimmer - You already know exactly how it will go: he will stand in the doorway for forty-five minutes explaining why the Romans stole their calendar from a civilisation that modern scholarship refuses to acknowledge, and somewhere in the middle of it he will say something that almost makes sense, and you will lose the thread of whatever you were thinking about before he knocked."

[=== ARCHITECTURE ===]
The kitchen cabinets are in the kitchen.
The handwritten note is on the table.

The cast-iron stove is in the kitchen.
The kitchen table is in the kitchen.
The chairs are in the kitchen.

Section - Pantry

Pantry is a room. "A small, cool pantry, its shelves lined with preserves and dry goods. A faint smell of must and vinegar. The single high window, fitted with an iron grille, lets in little light.[if the loose floorboard is open] One of the floorboards lies lifted, a dark gap beneath it.[end if] The kitchen lies to the east."

[=== ITEMS ===]
The description of the pantry shelves is "Rows of preserves and dry goods, neatly arranged. One of the shelves sits slightly uneven."
Understand "shelves", "shelf", "preserves" as the pantry shelves.

The loose floorboard is openable.
The loose floorboard is closed.
To say floorboard contents:
	if cloth bundle is in the loose floorboard:
		say " Inside it you see some items wrapped in an old oilcloth."
The description of the loose floorboard is "[if the loose floorboard is closed]One of the floorboards sits slightly proud of the others. You have always told yourself you would only lift it if things became truly desperate.[otherwise]One of the boards is lifted and reveals a hidden compartment.[floorboard contents][end if]"

Understand "floorboard", "floor", "board" as the loose floorboard.
Understand "lift [the loose floorboard]" as opening.

The cloth bundle is a container.
The cloth bundle is openable.
The cloth bundle is closed.
The cloth bundle is undescribed.
The description of the cloth bundle is "A cloth bundle containing a few letters bound with string – old ones, by the look of them, the ink faded. The kind you keep not because you should, but because you cannot bring yourself to burn them. A worn copy of the Neue Vorwärts. And the Luger."

After opening the cloth bundle:
	now the Luger is carried by the player;
	now the Neue Vorwärts is carried by the player;
	now the bundle of letters is carried by the player;
	now the cloth bundle is nowhere;
	say "You unwrap the bundle. Inside: a few letters, a worn copy of the Neue Vorwärts, and the Luger in its oilcloth."

The Neue Vorwärts is undescribed.
The description of the Neue Vorwärts is "A ... magazine."
Instead of reading the Neue Vorwärts:
	say "Exile voices, printed on cheap paper and smuggled across a border that keeps moving. You have read this issue already. You keep it anyway. At this point it is less about the articles than about the principle."

The bundle of letters is undescribed.
The description of the bundle of letters  is "A dozen letters, tied with the same piece of string for longer than is sensible. You know every name on every envelope. Some of those people have left the country. Some have not. You do not untie them."

The Luger is undescribed.
The Luger is wearable.
The description of the Luger is "A Luger P08, kept clean and loaded. The initials stamped into the grip are scratched out. You have carried it since Zurich, three years ago, when it still seemed like things might not come to this. They have come to this."
Understand "gun", "pistol", "luger" as the Luger.

[=== ARCHITECTURE ===]
The cloth bundle is in the loose floorboard.
The Neue Vorwärts is in the cloth bundle.
The bundle of letters is in the cloth bundle.
The Luger is in the cloth bundle.

The pantry shelves are scenery in the Pantry.
The loose floorboard is scenery in the Pantry.

Instead of opening the loose floorboard:
	now the loose floorboard is open;
	say "You lift the floorboard. Beneath it, wrapped in cloth, is everything you keep hidden."

Section - Dining Room

Dining Room is a room. "A formal dining room that sees little use. A large table surrounded by six chairs dominates the room, its surface bare and polished. A heavy sideboard stands against one wall, its glass doors displaying china that is rarely taken out. A lamp hangs low over the table, unlit. A window faces the street below. The hallway lies to the west."
Dining Room is east of Hallway.

Section - Bedroom

Bedroom is a room. "A quiet, orderly bedroom. A heavy wardrobe dominates one wall, its dark wood polished to a dull shine. The bed is neatly made, a single pillow at its head. On the nightstand, a small lamp and a well-worn paperback. A suitcase sits beneath the bed, just visible in the shadow. A window overlooks the rear courtyard. The hallway lies to the east."
Bedroom is west of Hallway.

